est candidate. We could argue that Candidate C's egocentric and communication issues may be a bigger risk for long-haul crew cooperation than B's pretentiousness. So we might still support C but suggest need for communication training. Or we could propose Candidate D as alternative because of strong problem solving and responsibility, but his moody and loner traits may affect crew cooperation.\n\nProbably maintain C but add nuance. However we need to bring new evidence not yet mentioned: we have note \"Candidate C puts concern for others above everything.\" That's a positive for crew cooperation. Also \"Candidate C has excellent attention skills.\" That's good for attention and accuracy. Those were not mentioned yet. So we can strengthen C's case.\n\nThus we can say: I still recommend C, and note his concern for others and excellent attention skills, which address crew cooperation and attention criteria, offsetting his communication difficulty.\n\nThus vote remains Candidate C.\n\nNow produce PUBLIC_MESSAGE and METADATA_JSON."}
